I've ascended 4 times so far.  And 3 out of those were thanks to an 
early wish.  One was thanks to an early wand of wishing.  But my second
ascension was wishless, and now I'm doing a polyless/wishless/genoless
elven ranger.  What I think is that while it's quite possible to ascend
without a great start, if you get one, your chances are going high up.
That's why many first ascensions are like you say, although I've read
at least one wishless YAFAP.  Another point is that when people get 
good gear at the beginning, they start thinking "oh, I can't lose this
character", and start being more careful.

